{"name":"Delicate Blue Mist","hex":"#bed7f0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rolls-Royce Silver Ghost","blocks":[{"text":"The Rolls-Royce Silver Ghost name refers both to a car model and one specific car from that series. Originally named the \"40/50 h.p.\" the chassis was first made at Royce's Manchester works, with production moving to Derby in July 1908, and also, between 1921 and 1926, in Springfield, Massachusetts, USA. Chassis no. 60551, registered AX 201, was the car that was originally given the name \"Silver Ghost\". Other 40/50 hp cars were also given names, but the Silver Ghost title was taken up by the press, and soon all 40/50s were called by the name, a fact not officially recognised by Rolls-Royce until 1925, when the Phantom range was launched."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost_at_Centenary.jpg/330px-Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost_at_Centenary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg/500px-Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg/1280px-Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg/500px-Rolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Claude Johnson at the wheel of AX201, the original \"Silver Ghost\", 1907","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARolls_Royce_Silver_Ghost_1907.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG/500px-1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG/1280px-1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG/500px-1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1920 Silver Ghost with limousine coachwork","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1920_Rolls-Royce_Silver_Ghost.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/RR40_50SG.jpg/500px-RR40_50SG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/RR40_50SG.jpg/1280px-RR40_50SG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/RR40_50SG.jpg/500px-RR40_50SG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"40/50 hp Silver Ghost7,428cc side-valve six-cylinder engine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARR40_50SG.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/T._E._Lawrence_in_Damascus_October_1918.jpg/330px-T._E._Lawrence_in_Damascus_October_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/T._E._Lawrence_in_Damascus_October_1918.jpg/330px-T._E._Lawrence_in_Damascus_October_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"T. E. Lawrence in Blue Mist, 1918","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AT._E._Lawrence_in_Damascus_October_1918.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg/250px-Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg/500px-Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg/250px-Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore2.jpg/250px-Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore2.jpg/500px-Rolls_Royce_Silverghost_AX201_restore2.jpg?utm_s